# "HUD" pipeline: futuristic, event-driven feedback. Loaded via
# `custom_shaders hud` in kitty.conf (kitty looks in <config>/shaders/).
#
# Every group has an animation_start, so a group that isn't animating isn't
# drawn at all: an idle terminal costs zero extra GPU work. Colors are Catppuccin
# Mocha converted to *linear* RGB (shaders work in linear light, not sRGB).
# animation_step 8 everywhere: the default is 50ms (20fps), which gave the
# 110ms spark ~2 frames; 8ms = 120Hz ProMotion, the floor set by repaint_delay.

# 1. Short cursor jumps leave a brief spark (hud-spark.slang: kitty's
#    lightning trail without forks/flicker, and silent on long jumps such as
#    switching split or tab, where it used to arc across both panes).
#    Subscribing to cursor-trail-move suppresses kitty's own trail renderer.
startgroup
    animation_start cursor-trail-move
    animation_stop cursor-trail-stop
    animation_step 8
    var float3 BOLT_COLOR = float3(0.610, 0.672, 0.905)
    var float3 GLOW_COLOR = float3(0.597, 0.381, 0.930)
    var float DURATION = 0.11
    var float JAGGEDNESS = 0.06
    var float GLOW_WIDTH = 4.5
    shaders hud-spark
endgroup

# 2. Changing split: the newly focused pane's edges glow in mauve, then fade
#    (300ms ease-out). hud-focus.slang adds light instead of multiplying it:
#    kitty's focus-highlight was invisible on this near-black background.
startgroup
    animation_start window-focus-in
    animation_stop 300
    animation_curve ease-out
    animation_step 8
    shaders hud-focus
endgroup

# 3. Changing tab: content sweeps in from the tab bar edge with a soft front
#    (hud-reveal.slang: kitty's tab-change wipe, minus dimming the tab bar and
#    minus starting from black -- see the comments there).
#    Kept at 120ms: the sweep hides part of the new tab until it ends, so at
#    220ms every tab switch *felt* slow even though nothing was computing. Same
#    length as tab_bar.py's crossfade so bar and content still move as one.
startgroup
    animation_start tab-change
    animation_stop 120
    animation_curve ease-out
    animation_step 8
    shaders hud-reveal
endgroup
